 'dateUpdated': '2026-07-10',
 'description': "She wasn't looking for him.\n"
                "He wasn't supposed to stay.\n"
                'But Lotte, the sharp-eyed café owner with a soft heart and no '
                'need for English, knew better.\n'
                '\n'
                'In a quiet Berlin café filled with secondhand furniture, old '
                "vinyl records, and Lotte's unbeatable cherry cake, Emi lives "
                'a life of stillness-small, steady, safe. Then Harry Styles '
                'walks in, quiet and unshaven, trying to disappear.\n'
                '\n'
                'What starts with shared glances and mismatched mugs becomes '
                'routines, soup bowls, and late-night confessions. Emi '
                "pretends not to know who he is. Harry pretends he's not "
                'falling. And Lotte? She sees everything-and starts nudging '
                'them together with cake, eye-rolls, and more than a little '
                'mischief.\n'
                '\n'
                "But secrets don't stay quiet forever. When the world comes "
                "calling and Harry's love songs start sounding a little too "
                'familiar, Emi has to choose: stay hidden in her quiet '
                'corners-or finally risk being seen.\n'
                '\n'
                'A slow-burn, aching love story about intimacy, anonymity, and '
                'the grandmotherly matchmaker who always knew best.\n'
                '\n'
                '---\n'
                "Warning : It's very slow and very long!",
